#. Add-on summary/title, usually the user visible name of the add-on
#. Translators: Summary/title for this add-on
#. to be shown on installation and add-on information found in add-on store
#: buildVars.py:21
msgid "Terminal Access for NVDA"
msgstr "Доступ до терміналу для NVDA"

# Long description to be shown for this add-on on add-on information from add-
# ons manager
#. Add-on description
#. Translators: Long description to be shown for this add-on on add-on information from add-on store
#: buildVars.py:24
msgid ""
"Provides enhanced terminal accessibility for Windows Terminal and "
"PowerShell, enabling screen reader users to efficiently navigate and "
"interact with command-line interfaces. Inspired by TDSR (Terminal Data "
"Structure Reader) and incorporates functionality from both TDSR and Speakup. "
"Advanced features inspired by community suggestions and discussions."
msgstr ""
"Забезпечує покращену доступність терміналу для Windows Terminal та "
"PowerShell, дозволяючи користувачам екранних зчитувачів ефективно "
"переміщатися та взаємодіяти з інтерфейсами командного рядка. Натхненний TDSR "
"(Terminal Data Structure Reader) та включає функціональність як TDSR, так і "
"Speakup. Розширені функції натхненні пропозиціями та обговореннями спільноти."

#. Brief changelog for this version
#. Translators: what's new content for the add-on version to be shown in the add-on store
#: buildVars.py:29
msgid ""
"v2.0.0-beta.15: the add-on is now pure Python. The native library and helper "
"process were removed after field testing showed the Python reads are faster "
"and more reliable, making the download much smaller and adding ARM64 "
"support. The \"Use native acceleration\" setting is gone. No feature changes."
msgstr ""

